  "body": "# 🔁 LifeOS 8.761.0: The One Loop\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/59c04882-92e1-490b-ab07-e84c2f46595f\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **One loop now runs at every level.** Every output climbs toward a written ideal state, and something checks whether it got there.\n\n**6,385 commits** · **426 issues and PRs closed** · **50 skills newly public (97 total)** · **2,050 new capabilities** · **18 hooks deleted**\n\n## ✨ What's new\n\n- 🎯 **Direction first.** Every ISA opens with a one-sentence ideal state you confirm *before* any code gets written.\n- 📏 **Assay checks everything.** Every criterion carries its own eval, and an unrun check reads as *unmeasured*, never as a pass.\n- 🧗 **HillClimb + Errata.** Your complaints get logged in your own words, then turned into experiments until a fix actually holds.\n- 🛠️ **Development skill.** Build, Test, Modify and Checkup, sized to the job: a one-file fix runs inline, a new project fans out.\n- ⏰ **Workflows in the cloud.** Scheduled jobs run whether or not your laptop is open, and \"remind me Friday\" just works.\n- 🚨 **Vigil.** One event log that texts you only when something actually matters.\n- 📊 **New Pulse.** A redesigned dashboard that opens on *Today*, and missing data shows as missing instead of fake green.\n- ⚡ **New statusline.** One process, refreshes every second, starts nothing.\n- 💬 **Text your DA.** The real DA over iMessage, with voice notes transcribed on your Mac and a passphrase-gated phone line.\n- 🔒 **Leaner security.** Claude Code's own permissions, git hooks and a kernel sandbox replace 18 noisy guard hooks. Your `.env` travels age-encrypted.\n- 📦 **One-command install or upgrade.** 7.x upgrades in place, backed up first, and nothing you wrote gets overwritten.\n- 🧠 **Fabric, rewritten.** 51 patterns beat the originals head to head and now replace them, plus new thinking skills: Superior, Unify, Simplify and Pareto.\n\n## 🚀 Upgrade\n\nHand `INSTALL.md` to your AI and say **\"install this\"**. Then run **`lifeos doctor`**.\n\n📖 The full notes, with every change explained: [Releases/v8.761.0/README.md](https://github.com/danielmiessler/LifeOS/blob/v8.761.0/Releases/v8.761.0/README.md)\n\n## 🙏 Thank you\n\nA big share of what got fixed came from your reports: @jlacour-git @bnkath2o @ebrett @jaylarr176 @xmasyx @CarbonRaven @DRAZY @schmetti-dev @mj-deving @GRyndStone @jacobo-ortiz @lgertel @hjbrandt @hjo20 @bytebyrobert @christianjgilman @pybe @Steffen025 @rogdex24 @ramazanpolat @maer @sabo961 @willhern829 @aveneri @cammcd @waveman2020-sudo @tzioup @spec-vova @Albyoung @rathko @dedafrost @0bsolescence @theNetworkChuck\n\n<details>\n<summary>All 426 closed issues and PRs</summary>\n\nCloses: #1580,#1584,#1606,#1614,#1665,#1712,#1721,#1732,#1754,#1755,#1777,#1781,#1787,#1788,#1789,#1790,#1791,#1792,#1793,#1794,#1795,#1796,#1797,#1798,#1799,#1800,#1801,#1802,#1803,#1804,#1805,#1806,#1807,#1808,#1809,#1810,#1811,#1812,#1813,#1814,#1815,#1816,#1817,#1818,#1820,#1821,#1824,#1825,#1827,#1828,#1829,#1830,#1831,#1832,#1833,#1834,#1835,#1837,#1838,#1839,#1840,#1841,#1842,#1843,#1844,#1845,#1846,#1848,#1849,#1850,#1851,#1852,#1853,#1854,#1855,#1856,#1857,#1858,#1859,#1860,#1861,#1862,#1863,#1864,#1865,#1866,#1867,#1868,#1869,#1870,#1871,#1872,#1873,#1874,#1875,#1876,#1877,#1878,#1879,#1880,#1881,#1882,#1883,#1884,#1885,#1886,#1887,#1888,#1889,#1891,#1892,#1893,#1894,#1895,#1896,#1897,#1898,#1899,#1901,#1902,#1903,#1904,#1905,#1906,#1907,#1908,#1909,#1910,#1911,#1912,#1913,#1914,#1915,#1916,#1917,#1918,#1919,#1920,#1921,#1922,#1923,#1924,#1925,#1926,#1927,#1929,#1930,#1931,#1932,#1933,#1934,#1935,#1936,#1937,#1938,#1939,#1940,#1941,#1942,#1943,#1944,#1945,#1946,#1947,#1948,#1949,#1950,#1951,#1952,#1953,#1954,#1955,#1956,#1957,#1958,#1959,#1960,#1961,#1962,#1963,#1964,#1965,#1966,#1967,#1968,#1969,#1970,#1971,#1972,#1973,#1974,#1975,#1976,#1977,#1978,#1979,#1980,#1982,#1983,#1984,#1985,#1986,#1987,#1988,#1989,#1990,#1991,#1992,#1993,#1994,#1995,#1996,#1997,#1998,#1999,